From 88f088a62f020d251740bbf63c517d5c70110584 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Senior Matthew <SeniorMatt@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 14:26:55 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 10/31] kcm_splashscreen: theme packages read in batches after
 the first frame, async previews, busy state
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Page type: Gallery (docs/page-design.md §5). Layout, config keys, Preview/Remove actions, Get New action unchanged
(already page action + per-card actions). NOT BUILT YET (owner stopped heavy work); checked statically only.

Changed:
- Empty/loading state: busy indicator only after 150 ms (HIG-ish "never block the first frame", design §3 Busy).
- Card thumbnails Image.asynchronous (design §5).
- Relabel table inventory/relabel/kcm_splashscreen.tsv (outer repo); no visible label changed, so no aliases needed.
  5 inventory rows kept, ksr markers added; inventory_check --kcm kcm_splashscreen --strict: 0 lost.

Speed (cause found in code, kcms/ksplash/kcm.cpp): load() ran in KCM load, listed every dir under
plasma/look-and-feel in all data paths, built a KPackage for each and tested filePath("splashmainscript"), all before the
page could show. Now load() only reads settings and adds the cheap "None" card; the package scan runs from
QTimer::singleShot(0) in ~8 ms batches (loadNextBatch, generation counter against a re-load), same order/filter.
themeChanged is emitted per batch with new rows so view.currentIndex finds the selected card when it arrives; the
"theme not in list -> defaults()" fallback now runs when the scan has finished. New property modelLoading.
After numbers: pending, manager will measure.

Not built yet; uncertain: the QML Timer/BusyIndicator are children of GridViewKCM (same as lookandfeel cf609d2);
repeated themeChanged emission per batch may re-evaluate SettingStateBinding (cheap).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01X5N5x9eWzmrq6QYrYLwQnk
